config DEFY_CONTROL
    bool
    depends on DEFY_HYBRID
    help
      The Neuron's control channel to each half, as dygma/defy_control.h
      describes it: the GATT service on each half, its client on the
      Neuron, and the Neuron's commands over the cable. DEFY_BATTERY,
      DEFY_LIGHTING and DEFY_HALF_VERSION select it for what they send
      over it.

config DEFY_BATTERY
    bool "Defy battery telemetry"
    default y
    depends on DEFY_HYBRID && BT
    select DEFY_CONTROL
    select DEFY_BATTERY_HCI if DEFY_BT_HCI_SPI
    help
      Each half's battery level and charger state, which its radio
      measures: the battery display's cells and the low-battery warning on the half's
      keys, and on the Neuron the lower of the halves' levels through the
      Bluetooth Battery Service. See docs/battery.md.

if DEFY_BATTERY

module = DEFY_BATTERY
module-str = Defy battery
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

endif

config DEFY_BATTERY_HCI
    bool
    depends on DEFY_BT_HCI_SPI
    select BT_HCI_VS_EVT_USER
    help
      The half's decoder of the radio's battery events,
      drivers/bluetooth/defy_battery_hci.c.

config DEFY_HALF_VERSION
    bool "Defy halves' version report"
    default y
    depends on DEFY_HYBRID && BT
    select DEFY_CONTROL
    select CRC
    help
      Each half reports its side, its program's CRC32 and seal version and
      the module version it was built from, in a third characteristic of
      its control service and in 'DV' cable frames. The Neuron keeps the
      latest report from each half for the half updater's HALF VERSIONS.
      See docs/versions.md.
